"""Editorial question designs for traditional clothing, puppetry, and games."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


TRADITIONAL_CLOTHING = """history_origins|A Garment's Documented History|What dated evidence shows how one garment form developed?|Name community and distinguish earliest artifact from absolute origin.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Garment Rechecked|Which features represent a local practice and which are exceptional?|Compare maker, wearer, occasion, and documented variants.
hidden_stories|The Makers Behind the Outfit|Whose spinning, dyeing, weaving, sewing, and care are overlooked?|Credit paid and unpaid work with consent.
beginner_explainers|Reading Clothing in Context|Who wears one form, when, and with what meaning?|Ask wearers and makers; avoid universal dress rules.
advanced_concepts|Continuity Through Design Change|How can materials or cut change while a form remains meaningful?|Compare dated examples and practitioner explanations.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Textile Attribution|Which evidence could identify a garment's maker or place?|Check fiber, technique, provenance, labels, and gaps.
technology_innovation|A New Loom or Dye|How did one tool change making or access?|Compare labor, output, price, quality, and maker control.
people_personalities|A Textile Maker's Contribution|How did one named maker transmit or adapt a skill?|Use consented biography within a wider workshop history.
major_events|Dress After a Policy Change|How did one law, migration, or market shock alter clothing?|Use dated records and wearer accounts.
how_it_works|From Fiber to Wearable Form|Which decisions shape one garment?|Trace fiber, dye, construction, fitting, use, and repair.
rise_fall|Demand for a Garment|What explains a measured change in making or wearing?|Check price, occasion, supply, fashion, and survey coverage.
then_vs_now|One Outfit Across Generations|How did cut, fabric, labor, and meaning change?|Use comparable objects and consented wearer accounts.
future_developments|Skills for the Next Generation|What would makers need to keep producing?|Ask about apprenticeships, materials, pay, rights, and demand.
myths_vs_facts|A Timeless Costume?|Which features are recent and which are documented earlier?|Date photographs, objects, and descriptions without ranking authenticity.
documentary_stories|A Garment Made and Worn|What happens between workshop and occasion?|Use maker and wearer consent; document cost and care.
creative_brief|Designing for a Named Occasion|Which practical and cultural requirements shape a garment?|State wearer preferences, permissions, climate, movement, and budget.
materials_and_tools|Why This Fiber and Tool|How do materials affect drape, durability, and labor?|Trace origin, properties, and maker choice.
process_breakdown|A Maker's Sequence|Where do skill and time enter spinning, dyeing, cutting, or weaving?|Observe with consent and quantify steps where possible.
composition_choice|Pattern and Silhouette|Why were particular colors, motifs, or proportions selected?|Ask the maker; avoid assigning symbolic meaning from appearance alone.
collaborative_authorship|Who Designed This Garment|How do maker, wearer, supplier, and inherited pattern contribute?|Attribute choices and compensation.
adaptation_across_media|From Garment to Image|What changes when clothing is photographed or marketed?|Compare fit, use, staging, editing, and consent.
audience_reception|How Wearers Interpret a Form|Do age or occasion alter its meaning?|Use varied consented accounts without treating one view as universal.
cultural_context|When Wearing Is Appropriate|Which community expectations govern a specific item?|Consult practitioners and note variation and restricted uses.
preservation_restoration|Caring for a Textile|Which repair or storage choice protects material and meaning?|Check fiber, dye, use, ownership, and conservation trade-offs.
rights_and_attribution|Credit for a Pattern|Who may reproduce or sell a design?|Trace maker consent, community claims, contracts, and law by jurisdiction.
style_comparison|Two Garments, Different Functions|Why do similar-looking forms serve different purposes?|Compare construction, wearers, context, and local names.
creative_failure|When a Design Did Not Work|What did makers change after a material or fit problem?|Use consented process records without sensationalizing error.
field_ingredient_or_fiber_origin|Following One Fiber|Where did a garment's fiber come from?|Trace producer, processing, trade, and uncertainty.
field_making_process|Time and Skill in One Piece|How is one garment actually made?|Document steps, labor hours, tools, and maker attribution.
field_cultural_context|A Garment in Use|What do wearers say its setting means?|Seek consent and avoid outsider symbolism.
field_consumer_claims|Testing an Authenticity Label|What does a seller's claim specify and prove?|Check origin, maker, method, price, and certification terms.
field_waste_and_reuse|After the Occasion|How is clothing repaired, reused, sold, or discarded?|Trace material life and local disposal context.
"""

DOLLS_PUPPETRY = """history_origins|A Puppet Form's Early Record|What dated evidence documents one local puppet tradition?|Separate earliest surviving object from first performance.
famous_examples|A Famous Puppet Character|What does one character mean in a complete show?|Compare repertoire, audience, venue, and performer accounts.
hidden_stories|Hands Behind the Puppet|Who carves, dresses, manipulates, voices, and repairs it?|Credit makers and performers, including collaborators.
beginner_explainers|How a Puppet Comes Alive|Which design and performance choices create movement?|Follow one named form and its local vocabulary.
advanced_concepts|Object and Performer Together|How do mechanism, voice, and audience change meaning?|Compare consented performances of the same puppet.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Puppet Attribution|Which clues could identify an object's maker or era?|Check material, construction, provenance, and archive gaps.
technology_innovation|A New Puppet Mechanism|Did one design expand movement or change labor?|Compare control, repair, weight, visibility, and cost.
people_personalities|A Puppeteer's Teaching Legacy|How did one practitioner transmit the form?|Use troupe records and apprentices' accounts with consent.
major_events|A Troupe After Disruption|How did one event alter routes, venues, or repertoire?|Use dated programs, financial records, and performer accounts.
how_it_works|From Workshop to Stage|What steps connect object making to performance?|Trace design, construction, rehearsal, transport, and show.
rise_fall|Puppet Shows Over Time|What explains a change in performances or apprentices?|Check venue, funding, audience, and recording definitions.
then_vs_now|A Puppet Form Across Generations|How did materials, stories, and audience interaction change?|Use dated objects and practitioner accounts.
future_developments|Keeping Puppetry Viable|Which resources do makers and performers prioritize?|Compare training, pay, venues, object care, and rights.
myths_vs_facts|A Fixed Ancient Character?|Which traits are documented early and which came later?|Compare scripts, objects, and performance memories.
documentary_stories|One Puppet's Working Life|How was an object made, used, repaired, and stored?|Use consented records and trace ownership.
creative_brief|Designing a Stage Puppet|What must one puppet do in a named scene?|Specify movement, sightlines, durability, maker and performer input.
materials_and_tools|A Puppet's Materials|Why choose wood, cloth, leather, or another material?|Compare weight, movement, cost, repair, and local availability.
process_breakdown|Building a Puppet|Which construction decisions enable expression?|Document joints, control, paint, costume, and testing with permission.
composition_choice|Shape, Color, and Gesture|How do visual choices read from the audience?|Ask makers and performers before assigning symbolic meaning.
collaborative_authorship|Who Created the Character|How do makers, scriptwriters, musicians, and manipulators share authorship?|Trace attribution and agreements.
adaptation_across_media|Stage Puppet to Screen|What changes when a live form is filmed?|Compare framing, timing, audience response, and rights.
audience_reception|A Puppet in Two Venues|How do different audiences respond?|Use consented observation and avoid treating one reaction as typical.
cultural_context|The Puppet's Social Role|When is a character comic, sacred, educational, or political?|Use practitioner explanations for a named setting.
preservation_restoration|Repairing a Working Puppet|When should conservation allow continued performance?|Compare maker wishes, fragility, replacement, and museum policy.
rights_and_attribution|Who May Reproduce a Puppet|What consent and rights attach to object and performance?|Check maker, troupe, community, and jurisdiction.
style_comparison|Two Puppet Mechanisms|How do hand, rod, string, or shadow forms change storytelling?|Compare actual objects, performer skill, and staging.
creative_failure|A Puppet That Would Not Move|What did makers learn from a design failure?|Use consented workshop records and show the revision.
field_community_ownership|Control of a Puppet Tradition|Who decides how a character may be shown?|Seek troupe and community consent for recording and reuse.
field_object_provenance|A Puppet in a Collection|How did it move from maker to current holder?|Trace custody, sale, donation, and disputed claims.
field_living_practice|A Full Puppet Performance|What differs from a museum display or short excerpt?|Observe with permission and document audience interaction.
field_conservation_choice|Object or Practice First|Which safeguarding choices do practitioners favor?|Compare repair, new making, apprenticeships, and archiving.
field_cultural_translation|Subtitling Puppet Dialogue|Which jokes or local references resist translation?|Check choices with performers and disclose limits.
"""

TRADITIONAL_GAMES = """history_origins|Early Record of a Local Game|What dated source describes its rules or setting?|Separate first record from an absolute invention date.
famous_examples|A Celebrated Traditional Game|How is it actually played by a named group?|Observe rules, equipment, age, place, and variation.
hidden_stories|Who Teaches the Game|Whose work maintains play spaces and skills?|Credit children, elders, makers, and organizers with consent.
beginner_explainers|Learning One Game|What does a new player need to know to join?|Explain aim, turn sequence, equipment, boundaries, and local variations.
advanced_concepts|Strategy Within Local Rules|Which decisions matter under one rule set?|Analyze game states and practitioner explanations.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Game Origin|Which similarities actually support a shared history?|Compare dated rules, travel routes, and evidence gaps.
technology_innovation|A Digital Version Tested|What changes when a physical game moves online?|Compare access, social play, rules, ownership, and learning.
people_personalities|A Game Keeper's Role|How did one teacher or organizer expand participation?|Use dated events and consented player accounts.
major_events|A Game After Losing Its Space|How did one land or policy change affect play?|Trace venue, rules, players, and community response.
how_it_works|A Round from Start to Finish|How do moves, scoring, and dispute resolution work?|Document one locally accepted rule set, not a universal version.
rise_fall|Participation in One Game|What evidence supports a revival or decline?|Check surveys, events, informal play, and changing labels.
then_vs_now|Rules Across Two Generations|Which rules and materials changed?|Compare dated descriptions and player memories.
future_developments|More Places to Play|Which conditions would support continued participation?|Ask players about space, safety, equipment, time, and teaching.
myths_vs_facts|Only One Correct Rulebook?|How many legitimate local variants exist?|Compare practitioner accounts and event rules.
documentary_stories|One Community Game Day|How do newcomers learn and experienced players negotiate?|Use consented observation and protect children.
creative_brief|Designing a Play Session|What must organizers provide for a specific group?|State space, age, materials, access, supervision, and consent.
materials_and_tools|Equipment of One Game|Why do players use a particular board, ball, or marker?|Trace materials, making, cost, and local substitutes.
process_breakdown|From Setup to Scoring|What sequence makes a match possible?|Document setup, turns, scoring, disputes, and reset.
composition_choice|Layout of the Play Space|How do dimensions and markings affect play?|Measure a local version and ask players about trade-offs.
collaborative_authorship|Who Sets the Rules|How do players, elders, clubs, and schools negotiate versions?|Trace decision records and living practice.
adaptation_across_media|Game to App or Stage|What social and physical features disappear?|Compare rules, pace, interaction, and rights.
audience_reception|Spectator and Player Views|How do participants value competition or cooperation?|Use varied accounts and observe actual sessions.
cultural_context|When the Game Is Played|How does it relate to season, ceremony, or daily life?|Use local player explanations, avoiding a universal claim.
preservation_restoration|Keeping Equipment Usable|Should an old board be repaired, copied, or stored?|Compare player needs, material fragility, and ownership.
rights_and_attribution|Credit for a Game Adaptation|Who should control a commercial version?|Check maker, community claims, licensing, and local law.
style_comparison|Two Related Rule Sets|Which change alters strategy or inclusion?|Run matched examples and consult practitioners.
creative_failure|A Rule That Excluded Players|What did organizers change after an access problem?|Use consented feedback and observed revision.
field_rules_design|Testing a Local Rule Set|Can a newcomer understand and apply it?|Watch an explained match and record ambiguities.
field_player_strategy|A Decision Point in Play|Why did a skilled player choose one move?|Use consented game records and alternative moves.
field_difficulty_curve|Learning Across Sessions|Which skills take longer to acquire?|Observe learners with consent; avoid fixed ability claims.
field_community_norms|Fair Play in Context|How do players handle disputes and etiquette?|Ask local participants and distinguish formal from informal rules.
field_accessibility_design|Who Can Join the Game|Which physical, sensory, cost, or language barriers exist?|Test adaptations with intended players and protect agency.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("247", "247_traditional_clothing", TRADITIONAL_CLOTHING,
                  "Traditional clothing through living makers, wearers, material supply, design change, and attribution.",
                  "dated garments and photographs with provenance, material and process records, sales claims, and consented maker and wearer accounts",
                  "Name community, garment, place, and period. Respect restricted uses and maker rights; do not treat one outfit as a timeless uniform or infer meaning from appearance alone.")
    revise_domain("250", "250_dolls_puppetry", DOLLS_PUPPETRY,
                  "Puppetry through object making, live performance, collaborative authorship, transmission, and care.",
                  "dated puppets and scripts with provenance, troupe records, full performance documentation, and consented maker, performer, and audience accounts",
                  "Name puppet form, troupe, place, and date. Obtain recording and reuse permission; distinguish a display object from living performance.")
    revise_domain("251", "251_traditional_games", TRADITIONAL_GAMES,
                  "Traditional games as locally varied rules, social play, material equipment, teaching, and access to space.",
                  "dated rule descriptions and equipment, consented observation of play, player and organizer accounts, and community safeguarding records",
                  "Name local rule set, player group, and place. Protect children in documentation; avoid presenting one version as universally correct.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
